    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Obsessive-compulsive disorder, partial response (F42.2)</content>. Y-BOCS 19, down 32 percent from 28: a partial response, just short of the 35 percent that defines response, after six weeks at 100 mg. Tolerating sertraline well. Suicide risk remains low. [S]<list><item>Increase sertraline to 150 mg each morning; nurse telephone check in two weeks.</item><item>Continue weekly ERP, focused on counting and repeating; therapist to rate the Y-BOCS at about week eighteen.</item><item>Collaborative safety plan reviewed and unchanged; 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline and the clinic number confirmed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Irritant hand dermatitis, resolved (L24.9)</content>. Healed with fewer washes and petrolatum. [S]<list><item>Petrolatum as needed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Underweight from food rituals (R63.6)</content>. 65.2 kg, BMI 18.4. [S]<list><item>Continue three meals a day.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Y-BOCS severity score (recorded in the note; no LOINC code found)</td><td>At baseline and about every 4 to 6 weeks during acute treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>19, down 32 percent from 28: partial response; dose increased to 150 mg</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide risk reassessment (C-SSRS Since Last Visit and PHQ-9 item 9 when given)</td><td>Every visit during acute treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No suicidal thoughts, intent, plan, or behavior since the last visit. Safety plan reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Sertraline adherence and adverse effects (nausea, diarrhea, sleep, activation, sexual effects)</td><td>Every visit and two weeks after each dose increase</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Nurse call two weeks after the last increase: two days of loose stools; no missed doses; dose increased to 150 mg with a nurse call in two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Exposure and response prevention attendance and homework</td><td>Every visit during acute treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Eleven sessions; handshake and most meals without calculating</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight and BMI</td><td>Every visit while underweight</td><td>Completed today</td><td>65.2 kg, BMI 18.4</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Hand skin</td><td>Every visit while dermatitis is present</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Healed</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Sleep diary</td><td>Every visit during acute treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>About five and a half hours a night</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Antipsychotic augmentation monitoring (weight, glucose, lipids, movement)</td><td>Only if an antipsychotic is added</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No augmentation; responding to sertraline and ERP</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Y-BOCS down by at least 35 percent (treatment response) by twenty-four weeks. In progress; target 1902-06-30 [S]</item><item>Rituals under one hour a day, with meals eaten without calculating. In progress; target 1902-06-30 [S]</item><item>BMI at least 18.5 with three meals a day. In progress; target 1902-06-30 [S]</item><item>Hands healed, with washing under 15 times a day. Outcome by 1902-04-07: Skin healed; washing about 12 times a day by twelve weeks [S]</item><item>At least six hours of sleep most nights. In progress; target 1902-06-30 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Patients With Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder (2007); Guideline Watch: Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Patients With Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder (2013); Obsessive-compulsive disorder and body dysmorphic disorder: treatment (CG31) (2005); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Nurse telephone check in two weeks; review in twelve weeks, after at least eight weeks at 150 mg. Next scheduled visit 1902-06-30: twenty-four-week OCD treatment review. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
